# Modus — every environment variable the backend reads.
#
# On Render, DATABASE_URL is provided by the blueprint (render.yaml); set the secrets
# below in the dashboard, never in the repository. Locally, copy what you need into
# your shell or a .env your process manager reads (.env is git-ignored).
#
# Leave DATABASE_URL unset locally to use a throwaway SQLite file instead of Postgres.

# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host:5432/dbname

# ---- The tenant this deployment serves ---------------------------------------
# One deployment serves one tenant today. Its data is loaded from a package
# (POST /api/admin/tenant/import); its name, team word, currency and country live in
# the configuration's `tenant` block, not here. Default: "default".
# TENANT_ID=default

# ---- HERE routing (required for baking geometry) ----------------------------
# Called server-side only; the key never reaches a browser. Check that your HERE plan
# covers your use (the Base Plan lists excluded use cases).
# HERE_API_KEY=...

# ---- Mapbox public token (recommended) ---------------------------------------
# A browser (pk.) token — public by design. Used by the staff app's maps and the PDF's
# static map; map/config.js carries the route map's own copy. Restrict it to your
# domains in the Mapbox account.
# MAPBOX_TOKEN=pk....

# ---- Admin protection ------------------------------------------------------
# While ADMIN_TOKEN is unset, _check_admin() is a no-op and EVERY admin endpoint is
# open — including the ones that spend HERE calls per click and the Config save that
# rewrites every payload and cycle time.
#
# ⚠️ THE VALUE IS THE OUTPUT OF THE COMMAND, NOT THE COMMAND. A deployment has been
# found with ADMIN_TOKEN set to the literal text "openssl rand -hex 24" because a
# comment like this one read as if that were the value. It is not. Run it:
#
#     openssl rand -hex 24        (macOS / Linux / Git Bash)
#
# and paste the 48-character hex string it PRINTS — something like 3f9a1c... — here
# and into the admin token field on the Routes page. Never paste the command itself.
# ADMIN_TOKEN=

# ---- Google Street View (Phase 2.5a, optional) ------------------------------
# Street View imagery in location popups. Entirely optional: with no key set, the
# popups simply show no photo and nothing else changes.
#
# This is Google Maps Platform — a SEPARATE product, key and bill from HERE. Enable
# only the "Street View Static API" for this key and restrict it to your server's IP.
# The key is held by the backend and never sent to the browser.
#
# Cost: metadata lookups are free and consume no quota; IMAGES are billable. The app
# always checks metadata first and never requests an image for a location Google has
# no imagery for. Read the current rate off Google's pricing page — it has changed
# twice recently, so no figure is quoted anywhere in this repo.
# GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# Optional but recommended: Google's URL signing secret. With it set, requests are
# signed so a leaked key cannot be used elsewhere. Without it, everything still works.
# GOOGLE_MAPS_URL_SIGNING_SECRET=

# ---- Country services (nothing to configure here) ------------------------------
# Switched on by the tenant's country (the `tenant.country` setting on Config):
#   EE      road restrictions from the Estonian Transport Administration (Tark Tee),
#           fetched server-side and cached for 30 minutes; the Maa-amet orthophoto;
#           Estonian vehicle labels. No key needed.
#   EU-27   the diesel price from the EU Weekly Oil Bulletin, fetched server-side.
#   others  no restriction layer; the diesel price is typed by an admin on Config.

# ---- Access codes (checked by the server) ---------------------------------------
# A team code sees only forecast lines of that team and cannot approve. The variable
# names keep the internal slot ids IPT1…IPT6; people see the tenant's own team names.
# PLANNER_CODE sees every team and approves. ADMIN_CODE is planner plus the admin
# surface, which STILL needs ADMIN_TOKEN for /api/admin/*.
# IPT1_CODE=
# IPT2_CODE=
# IPT3_CODE=
# IPT4_CODE=
# IPT5_CODE=
# IPT6_CODE=
# PLANNER_CODE=
# ADMIN_CODE=

# ---- The demo codes are OPT-IN, and sign-in FAILS CLOSED -------------------------
# submitter123 / planner123 / admin123 are well-known strings. The server honours them
# only when you ask for them here AND no real code is set; the sign-in box never names
# them.
#
#   codes set above          → those codes, and ONLY those. This line is ignored.
#   nothing set, no opt-in   → nobody signs in at all. (Like MAP_PASSWORD, not ADMIN_TOKEN.)
#   nothing set, opt-in on   → the three demo codes work. Local checkouts only.
#
# ⚠️ DO NOT SET THIS ON RENDER. Truthy values are 1 / true / yes / on; a variable created
# and left blank counts as off, on purpose.
# ALLOW_DEMO_CODES=1

# ---- The /map/ password and the /help/ staff gate ------------------------------
# /map/ and /help/ are gated, with DIFFERENT keys, because they have different
# audiences.
#
#   /map/    a SHARED PASSWORD (below). Give the string to a stakeholder or a client
#            and they see the corridor without an account.
#   /help/   the STAFF SIGN-IN only. Nothing to configure — it follows the access codes.
#
# ⚠️ THIS FAILS CLOSED, UNLIKE ADMIN_TOKEN. With MAP_PASSWORD unset, an outside visitor
# to /map/ is REFUSED and told the map is not configured. Your own team is unaffected:
# a valid access code, or the cookie a staff sign-in sets, opens the map whether or not
# a password exists. A forgotten MAP_PASSWORD costs you external viewers, never staff.
#
# ⚠️ ROTATING THIS SIGNS EVERYONE OUT. The cookie is signed with a key derived from the
# password, so changing it invalidates every cookie already issued. That is the feature:
# it is how you take access away from someone who should no longer have it.
# MAP_PASSWORD=

# Optional. Set an explicit signing key and the cookie survives a password rotation —
# useful if you rotate the password often and do NOT want to sign everyone out.
# Leave unset and the key is derived from MAP_PASSWORD + ADMIN_TOKEN.
# GATE_SECRET=

# Local development only. MAP_GATE=off reopens BOTH /map/ and /help/ with no password.
# Anything other than off / 0 / false / no leaves the gate ON, including leaving it unset.
# MAP_GATE=off
